          "crates/node-native/src/traffic_store.rs:163"
        ],
        "note": "The first two crash cases observe the renamed file contents. The source fsyncs its data before rename, but the name can be visible before the following directory fsync returns. These process-kill cases therefore do not independently acknowledge completion of the full checkpoint transaction or test power-loss durability. Successful frozen-snapshot and quiescence RPCs do await the complete commit. This is an execution-evidence boundary, not a defect in the source publication order.",
        "suggestion": "Describe the first two cases as observed fsynced file data surviving process SIGKILL. If a future claim requires independently confirmed completed periodic checkpoints or power-loss resilience, add an explicit completion barrier or storage-fault experiment and bind that new version."
